      <Placemark>
        <name>EGD123 IMBER</name>
        <description><![CDATA[511724N 0020107W -<br>511339N 0015746W -<br>511348N 0015705W -<br>511023N 0015325W -<br>511006N 0015702W -<br>511106N 0020713W -<br>511329N 0021149W -<br>511516N 0020939W -<br>511705N 0020312W -<br>511724N 0020107W <br>Upper limit: 50000 FT ALT<br>Lower limit: SFC AMC Manageable.<br><br>Vertical Limit 3000 FT ALT H24.<br><br>Vertical Limit 23,000 FT ALT Mon-Thu 0800-2359 (0700-2300), Fri 0800-1730 (0700-1630).<br><br>Vertical Limit OCNL notified to altitudes up to 50,000 FT ALT by NOTAM.<br><br>Activity:  Ordnance, Munitions and Explosives / Para Dropping / Unmanned Aircraft System (UAS) / Electronic/Optical Hazards.<br><br>Service: SUACS: Boscombe Down ATC on 126.705 when open; SUAAIS: Salisbury Information on 122.755 when open; at other times SUAAIS via London Information on 124.750 MHz.<br><br>Contact: Pre-flight information / Booking: SPTA Air Operations, Tel: 01980-674710 or 674730 when open.<br><br>SI 1963/1293, SI 1981/1882. Aircraft approved into Danger Areas out of hours are to make blind calls on VHF 122.755. This is a common channel also used by Pembrey, Holbeach and Donna Nook AWRs - ensure calls are specific to SPTA Danger Areas.<br><br>SUA Authority: DAATM (DIO).]]></description>
